WEBVTT

00:00.377 --> 00:03.708
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.709 --> 00:07.011
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.012 --> 00:10.582
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.583 --> 00:13.585
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.586 --> 00:17.088
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.089 --> 00:20.425
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.426 --> 00:21.993
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:21.994 --> 00:23.328
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.329 --> 00:28.932
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:29.382 --> 00:33.647
<b><font color="#ff0000">Sync and corrections by btsix
www.addic7ed.com</font></b>

00:33.872 --> 00:36.407
And now, the Game Show Network presents,

00:36.408 --> 00:39.811
<i>Are We Talking About Jake
Gyllenhaal or Jared Leto?</i>

00:40.033 --> 00:43.100
"I am oily-haired with
dinner-plate eyes."

00:44.182 --> 00:46.849
"I was in that one movie
about the weirdo."

00:48.053 --> 00:51.354
"I somehow look both
deathly ill and ripped."

00:52.358 --> 00:56.105
"I am a less successful
version of Tobey Maguire."

00:56.106 --> 00:57.829
Anyone? No?

00:57.830 --> 01:02.700
"You would totally believe any
story about me being a dick."

01:02.701 --> 01:04.802
I'm changing the channel.
I like both of them.

01:04.803 --> 01:06.237
Peter, did you see this?

01:06.238 --> 01:07.805
It says here that Carter Pewterschmidt

01:07.806 --> 01:10.319
has bought the
Pawtucket Patriot Brewery.

01:10.320 --> 01:11.133
Now what's that?

01:11.134 --> 01:12.543
It's where you work, Peter.

01:12.544 --> 01:14.612
Why the hell would Daddy
buy the brewery?

01:14.613 --> 01:16.714
Well, there's children in the
room... watch your swearing...

01:16.715 --> 01:19.450
But apparently, he's looking
to diversify his holdings.

01:19.451 --> 01:23.123
Wow, Dad. I guess that means
Grandpa's your new boss.

01:23.124 --> 01:24.895
Ah, crap. I don't want to work for him.

01:24.896 --> 01:27.191
I'd rather work for Doctor Frankenstein.

01:32.331 --> 01:34.924
- Igor, I did it!
- Hold on.

01:34.925 --> 01:37.068
You discovered the power
to create new life,

01:37.069 --> 01:39.037
and you created a guy?

01:39.038 --> 01:43.184
So I should've made a woman so
I could have sex with a corpse?

01:43.185 --> 01:44.008
I don't know, man.

01:44.009 --> 01:46.410
You just shouldn't have made a guy.

01:51.750 --> 01:53.584
All right, now that
I'm in charge of this brewery,

01:53.585 --> 01:55.153
there's gonna be some changes
around here.

01:55.154 --> 01:59.123
For one thing, no more T-shirts
or dungarees in the work place.

01:59.757 --> 02:01.196
Dungarees are jeans!

02:02.116 --> 02:03.795
Griffin? What are you doing here?

02:03.796 --> 02:05.296
I... I work here.

02:05.297 --> 02:06.898
You do? No way!

02:06.899 --> 02:08.666
Oh, this is gonna be fun.

02:08.667 --> 02:10.902
Effective immediately,
you're the guy at the office

02:10.903 --> 02:13.871
with a weird ski tan, but
you can't talk about it.

02:13.872 --> 02:15.707
Hey, what, did you go
skiing this weekend?

02:15.708 --> 02:17.708
I'm not allowed to talk about it.

02:27.820 --> 02:29.152
Aw, damn it.

02:31.656 --> 02:33.090
Morning, Brian.

02:33.092 --> 02:34.158
I'm afraid you ran a red light.

02:34.159 --> 02:35.693
Your license please.

02:35.694 --> 02:36.928
Ugh. I swear, Joe,

02:36.929 --> 02:39.230
the light was still gray
when I went through it.

02:39.231 --> 02:41.631
Mm-hmm. Are you aware this is expired?

02:41.633 --> 02:42.133
What?

02:42.134 --> 02:43.735
Brian, step out of the vehicle.

02:43.736 --> 02:45.036
Wha-Wha... What? What's going on?

02:45.037 --> 02:46.437
Well, the law's clear.

02:46.438 --> 02:47.872
I have to confiscate your license,

02:47.873 --> 02:49.507
and you're gonna have to walk home.

02:49.508 --> 02:51.175
Well, can't you at least give me a ride?

02:51.176 --> 02:52.710
No can do, amigo.

02:52.711 --> 02:54.911
Ugh. All right, I guess
I'll just call an Uber.

02:58.684 --> 03:01.752
Are you Brian?

03:06.369 --> 03:08.025
Ah, Griffin, there you are.

03:08.026 --> 03:09.894
I've decided that as your new boss,

03:09.895 --> 03:12.497
I'm gonna require you to
have a standing desk.

03:12.498 --> 03:14.665
Aw, but I'll look like such an ass!

03:14.666 --> 03:15.967
And that's not all.

03:15.968 --> 03:17.635
You got to constantly tell everybody

03:17.636 --> 03:20.271
what a good idea it is,
and how important it is,

03:20.272 --> 03:22.540
and how wrong they are
for having traditional desks.

03:22.541 --> 03:24.876
Can't I just work at it
and mind my own business?

03:24.877 --> 03:26.677
No, you have to be a freak about it.

03:26.678 --> 03:28.813
Maybe it can just be
my own personal choice,

03:28.814 --> 03:30.982
and-and I'm not judging
others for their choices.

03:30.983 --> 03:33.317
No. You being right means
everyone else is wrong.

03:33.318 --> 03:36.320
That's what your standing desk
is saying to the chair people.

03:36.321 --> 03:38.489
From now on,
you call them "chair people."

03:38.490 --> 03:40.576
Oh, and three times
a day you have to say,

03:40.577 --> 03:42.994
"Sitting is the biggest killer
in America."

03:54.592 --> 03:55.773
Good night, Peter.

03:55.774 --> 03:57.575
Good night,
gender-transitioned co-worker

03:57.576 --> 03:59.254
we had a whole meeting about.

04:00.078 --> 04:03.714
Mr. Pewterschmidt, what
you're ordering is illegal.

04:03.715 --> 04:05.025
I don't care about that.

04:05.026 --> 04:07.752
I want our beer cans made from
the cheapest material possible.

04:07.753 --> 04:08.413
But sir...

04:08.414 --> 04:11.084
What about those metal toilets
where prisoners make wine?

04:11.085 --> 04:12.030
Use those.

04:12.765 --> 04:15.126
But sir, if word got out
about this, it'd be one

04:15.127 --> 04:17.762
of the most notorious
developments in beer history,

04:17.763 --> 04:21.968
second only to Michelob Ultra
Dragon Fruit Peach.

04:27.840 --> 04:31.242
Peter, are you sure you heard
Mr. Pewterschmidt correctly?

04:31.243 --> 04:34.512
He actually said
he wanted cheap, toxic materials

04:34.513 --> 04:37.248
inserted into the brewery's
supply stream?

04:37.249 --> 04:38.483
Well, his eyes looked different

04:38.484 --> 04:40.518
how he said it, but that was the gist.

04:40.519 --> 04:42.987
Also, some of the brewery
workers say very hurtful things

04:42.988 --> 04:45.065
if a co-worker wears shorts.

04:45.066 --> 04:46.123
Follow the money.

04:46.124 --> 04:47.592
Mr. Griffin, it sounds like

04:47.593 --> 04:49.760
you've brought me an interesting story.

04:49.761 --> 04:51.762
What should I do with it, Ollie?

04:51.763 --> 04:52.964
Make it news!

04:52.965 --> 04:54.732
Ah, you got a standing desk, too?

04:54.733 --> 04:55.967
Sitting's bad!

04:55.968 --> 04:57.697
I know. They don't want
to hear it, though.

05:03.141 --> 05:05.643
Sir, there's
a reporter here to see you.

05:05.644 --> 05:08.179
Is it Kermit the Frog
when he's wearing a trench coat?

05:08.180 --> 05:09.981
That tells you he's a reporter.

05:23.228 --> 05:26.264
Sir, an anonymous whistleblower
in the brewery says

05:26.265 --> 05:28.733
you've personally ordered
the sourcing of cut-rate,

05:28.734 --> 05:31.749
potentially toxic canning materials.

05:31.750 --> 05:33.121
God, you're gorgeous.

05:33.122 --> 05:36.374
Mr. Pewterschmidt, I remind you,
this is on the record.

05:36.375 --> 05:38.910
You ever been with a man
who's got a prostate

05:38.911 --> 05:41.397
the size of a beefsteak tomato?

05:51.404 --> 05:53.127
Oh, crap, it's Carter!

05:53.128 --> 05:54.821
I bet he's mad
I told the news about him.

05:54.822 --> 05:56.693
I'll just do what Superman does.

05:58.297 --> 05:59.776
Oh, hey, Carter.

05:59.777 --> 06:01.722
Hello, citizen. Have you seen Peter?

06:01.723 --> 06:04.468
Aw, he was just here!

06:04.469 --> 06:05.670
Daddy, what's this about?

06:05.671 --> 06:07.405
Did Peter screw something up at work?

06:07.406 --> 06:09.473
No, I'm here because
I've got important news.

06:09.474 --> 06:12.662
Lois, everyone, I've left your mother,

06:12.663 --> 06:14.896
and Tricia Takanawa
is moving in with me.

06:14.897 --> 06:16.742
Holy crap! What?!

06:16.743 --> 06:17.748
I wanted you to know.

06:18.095 --> 06:19.796
I'm in love!

06:19.797 --> 06:21.731
Well, good for you
for being honest, Carter.

06:21.732 --> 06:22.999
It's never good

06:23.000 --> 06:25.068
to keep something
that matters to you a secret.

06:25.069 --> 06:27.170
<i>Tell her about the surf camp
in Belize, Peter.</i>

06:27.171 --> 06:28.395
<i>Tell her you're going.</i>

06:28.396 --> 06:30.296
<i>Tell her it's your dream,
and you deserve it.</i>

06:30.297 --> 06:32.098
<i>Tell her it'll make you a better father.</i>

06:32.099 --> 06:33.433
What's that, Peter?

06:33.434 --> 06:35.621
Ah, nothing. Just something stupid.

06:53.266 --> 06:55.534
You're leaving Babs
for Tricia Takanawa?!

06:55.535 --> 06:57.503
And I've never been happier!

06:57.504 --> 06:59.338
What about Mom? Where is Mom?

06:59.339 --> 07:02.116
The sanitarium. The sanitarium?!

07:02.117 --> 07:03.757
Yeah. I told her I was leaving her,

07:03.758 --> 07:05.392
and she freaked out for no reason.

07:05.393 --> 07:07.987
And I'll tell you, I don't know
why they call it a "sanitarium."

07:08.001 --> 07:09.568
That place is a filthy hell hole.

07:09.569 --> 07:11.570
Oh, my God! That's awful!

07:11.571 --> 07:14.239
Sorry. What'd you say?
I was texting Tricia.

07:14.240 --> 07:16.475
She just sent me
a picture of her smoothie.

07:16.476 --> 07:19.116
"Looks good, babe."

07:23.116 --> 07:24.883
All right, class, let's get started.

07:24.884 --> 07:26.318
Stewie, what are you doing?

07:26.319 --> 07:27.786
And why are you dressed like that?

07:27.787 --> 07:30.055
Because I'm your driver's
ed instructor, Brian.

07:30.056 --> 07:31.323
- You're what?
- That's right.

07:31.324 --> 07:32.658
I heard you lost your license,

07:32.659 --> 07:34.293
and I'm gonna help you get it back.

07:34.294 --> 07:35.861
Uh... okay.

07:35.862 --> 07:37.563
Now, we've got a lot to cover.

07:37.564 --> 07:39.531
But first, let's watch a safety video

07:39.532 --> 07:42.667
designed to terrorize you into
being a responsible motorist.

07:48.074 --> 07:50.275
Come on, kid with a bright future.

07:50.276 --> 07:52.811
I'll give you a no-seatbelt car ride

07:52.812 --> 07:55.314
after this teen kegger party.

07:55.315 --> 07:56.515
I don't know.

07:56.516 --> 07:58.350
I'm going to Harvard-Yale tomorrow.

07:58.351 --> 08:00.852
I'd hate to lose it all
because of making poor choices.

08:00.853 --> 08:04.323
Ah, come on, man. I just had
a couple of alcohol beers.

08:04.324 --> 08:07.059
And I'm his girlfriend
'cause he has great genitals.

08:07.060 --> 08:09.394
And I'm impressed
with reckless behavior,

08:09.395 --> 08:12.798
so I'm going to reward him with
my mouth while he's driving.

08:12.799 --> 08:15.167
Now let's smoke a marijuana cigarette

08:15.168 --> 08:17.202
while I'm speeding because of a dare.

08:17.203 --> 08:20.038
Hey, careful. I'd hate
for you to be unresponsive

08:20.039 --> 08:23.775
to my pleasuring while you're
driving because of intoxication.

08:23.776 --> 08:25.143
Stewie, is this about anything

08:25.144 --> 08:26.545
but oral stuff while you're driving?

08:26.546 --> 08:28.680
It's about all facets
of driving safety, yes.

08:28.681 --> 08:29.948
I'm gonna fast-forward.

08:34.454 --> 08:36.188
What a waste.

08:36.189 --> 08:38.624
I'm a grizzled, seen-it-all veteran cop,

08:38.625 --> 08:41.460
and I'm shaking my head
at the senseless waste.

08:41.461 --> 08:43.462
Sir, we've done our police tests.

08:43.463 --> 08:45.030
The driver was being mouth-pleased

08:45.031 --> 08:46.931
at the moment of impact.

08:54.507 --> 08:56.074
Lois! Fat Ass!

08:56.075 --> 08:59.077
Family, I want you to
meet Tricia Takanawa.

08:59.078 --> 09:02.381
Hello, everyone. So happy you came.

09:02.382 --> 09:03.715
Yup, food's on the table,

09:03.716 --> 09:05.417
and if anyone needs
some dirty underpants,

09:05.418 --> 09:06.885
the vending machine's right over there.

09:06.886 --> 09:08.186
How nice.

09:08.187 --> 09:09.855
Right where my mother's
China cabinet used to be.

09:09.856 --> 09:12.557
Lois, can I please have a dollar
for the vending machine?

09:12.558 --> 09:14.526
No, Peter. I'm getting our coats.

09:14.527 --> 09:16.260
We're leaving.

09:20.767 --> 09:22.534
No! Bill too crinkly!

09:22.535 --> 09:24.502
Try again!

09:25.805 --> 09:27.339
Bill too crinkly!

09:27.340 --> 09:29.341
You dollar funny!

09:29.342 --> 09:31.376
This must be so difficult for you.

09:31.377 --> 09:34.056
It is. There's a lot of choices here.

09:34.057 --> 09:35.213
But I ain't talking to you.

09:35.214 --> 09:37.816
I thought you were supposed to
be doing a news story on Carter,

09:37.817 --> 09:39.284
not shacking up with him.

09:39.285 --> 09:41.720
The truth is all I ever wanted

09:41.721 --> 09:43.822
was to some day have a family of my own.

09:43.823 --> 09:47.192
And I realized Carter
could give me all of that.

09:47.193 --> 09:48.794
A family all your own?

09:48.795 --> 09:50.962
Yes. A family just like this,

09:50.963 --> 09:54.066
in fact, with a fine son
just like you, Peter.

09:54.067 --> 09:57.836
A son to whom I could one day
give a piece of sour plum candy.

09:58.830 --> 10:00.441
Thank you, Mama Tricia!

10:00.442 --> 10:03.642
But a lazy son
who does not make me proud?

10:03.643 --> 10:06.945
Peter, that son deserves no candy.

10:08.881 --> 10:10.215
I swear, Mama Tricia,

10:10.216 --> 10:13.027
I'm gonna make you the
proudest Tiger Mom of all!

10:13.028 --> 10:15.554
Not like how Jesus feels about his kid.

10:15.555 --> 10:17.723
Dad, I got bullied at school!

10:17.724 --> 10:19.391
They flipped up my lunch tray!

10:19.392 --> 10:20.859
Oh, that sucks.

10:20.860 --> 10:22.561
I wonder if that's the worst thing

10:22.562 --> 10:24.629
that ever happened to a guy?

10:24.630 --> 10:26.832
Whoa. Whoa!

10:26.833 --> 10:28.500
Billy, this guy in this book here...

10:28.501 --> 10:31.610
He's really getting
the business... yikes!

10:31.611 --> 10:34.061
Okay, I'm sorry. What
happened at school today?

10:34.062 --> 10:35.607
You're kind of a dick, Dad.

10:35.608 --> 10:37.876
Huh. I wonder if there's anyone in here

10:37.877 --> 10:39.678
whose dad was a bigger dick.

10:39.679 --> 10:42.279
Wow! Crazy!

10:45.852 --> 10:48.820
Uh, Mom, why is Dad
over there playing chess

10:48.821 --> 10:50.422
with Tricia Takanawa?

10:50.423 --> 10:52.524
Because, Chris, your idiot father

10:52.525 --> 10:54.259
thinks she's his new "Tiger Mom,"

10:54.260 --> 10:56.094
and he's trying to impress her.

10:56.095 --> 10:59.331
All right, Peter, it's time
to master the game of chess.

10:59.332 --> 11:00.732
Okay, that shouldn't be too hard.

11:00.733 --> 11:03.535
No. You will do it in the
traditional Japanese way...

11:03.536 --> 11:05.937
On a wacky game show
while a beautiful woman

11:05.938 --> 11:08.340
beats your scrotum with a reed.

11:08.341 --> 11:10.675
Ow. I don't know which way
the horse goes.

11:12.412 --> 11:14.778
Why is that guy laughing at me
and where is he?

11:15.548 --> 11:18.049
There was a time limit?
Nobody told me that.

11:19.485 --> 11:21.787
Time for "Good Door, Bad Door"!

11:21.788 --> 11:24.456
Wait. How bad is the bad door?

11:26.626 --> 11:29.027
Grandpa-san, how bad was the bad door?

11:29.028 --> 11:30.429
Not too bad.

11:30.430 --> 11:31.830
But shortly afterwards,

11:31.831 --> 11:33.665
I was almost eaten alive
by an escalator.

11:34.934 --> 11:36.735
The game is still going on?

11:36.736 --> 11:40.338
You lose chess!

11:45.011 --> 11:47.913
Peter, another way
to impress your Asian Tiger Mom

11:47.914 --> 11:50.348
is to put on this
old-fashioned baseball hat

11:50.349 --> 11:53.185
and assist Indiana Jones
on his next adventure.

11:53.186 --> 11:54.886
You got it, Mama Tricia.

11:54.887 --> 11:56.988
Okay, nice and slow, Doctor Jones.

11:56.989 --> 11:58.957
More alcohol and pot.

11:58.958 --> 12:01.159
Yeah, let's get you out
of the tub first, Doctor Jones.

12:01.160 --> 12:02.994
I want to fly an old plane.

12:02.995 --> 12:04.463
I'm not sure that's a great idea.

12:04.464 --> 12:05.897
Not a new, safe one.

12:05.898 --> 12:07.299
Uh, yeah, yeah, I got that.

12:07.300 --> 12:09.334
There's a
skeleton in my bedroom.

12:09.335 --> 12:10.836
That's your wife, Doctor Jones.

12:10.837 --> 12:13.104
Now maybe today we don't do the earring?

12:13.105 --> 12:15.639
No. Earring every day.

12:18.845 --> 12:20.212
All right, Brian, let's begin.

12:20.213 --> 12:21.546
Great, let's do it.

12:21.547 --> 12:22.681
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

12:22.682 --> 12:24.456
Stop! Demerit!

12:24.457 --> 12:25.317
What the hell?

12:25.318 --> 12:26.585
Where are your hands, Brian?

12:26.586 --> 12:28.153
Uh... on the steering wheel?

12:28.154 --> 12:29.954
Ten and two.

12:32.091 --> 12:33.926
All right, commence.

12:35.294 --> 12:37.362
IPDE, Brian, IPDE. What?

12:37.363 --> 12:40.899
IPDE... Identify,
Predict, Decide, Execute.

12:40.900 --> 12:43.068
You've got to constantly
be IPDE-ing everything

12:43.069 --> 12:44.536
in your target zone.

12:44.537 --> 12:45.971
I-I-I-I don't, I don't know
what you're saying.

12:45.972 --> 12:47.405
"Identify. Predict..."

12:47.406 --> 12:48.707
Yeah, you said that.

12:48.708 --> 12:50.108
- But it doesn't mean anyth...
- IPDE that.

12:50.109 --> 12:52.744
- Uh... it's a child with a ball.
- Very good.

12:52.745 --> 12:55.013
Identified. Now predict.

12:55.014 --> 12:56.648
- Predict what?
- IPDE.

12:56.649 --> 12:58.350
Yeah, you keep saying
that like it's a word.

12:58.351 --> 12:59.885
Those four letters don't make a word.

12:59.886 --> 13:01.753
It-it's not helping
me remember anything.

13:01.754 --> 13:03.388
Well, now you've got
an oncoming vehicle.

13:03.389 --> 13:05.357
Pay attention to your
four-to-six second zone.

13:05.358 --> 13:07.392
What? What is that?
Fo-four-to-six second...?

13:07.393 --> 13:08.860
IPDE the car, Brian. IPDE the car!

13:08.861 --> 13:10.061
What does that mean?

13:10.062 --> 13:11.596
Now, check your gauges with one eye

13:11.597 --> 13:13.265
while keeping
your other eye on the road.

13:13.266 --> 13:14.666
My eyes go in the same direction.

13:14.667 --> 13:16.034
What's your tire pressure?

13:16.035 --> 13:17.702
I-I can't... I don't...
I-I'm in the car.

13:17.703 --> 13:19.037
Stop! Demerit!

13:19.038 --> 13:20.472
Stewie, I know how to drive.

13:20.473 --> 13:21.773
I've been driving for years.

13:22.909 --> 13:26.411
Ever hear of IPDE, jackass?

13:30.917 --> 13:33.385
I had a great day with the fat son.

13:33.386 --> 13:35.320
He's started to respond positively

13:35.321 --> 13:37.556
to the caning
of his buttocks and knuckles.

13:37.557 --> 13:39.324
Speaking of buttocks and knuckles,

13:39.325 --> 13:40.992
let's fool around.

13:40.993 --> 13:43.395
Mmm, sounds good.

13:43.396 --> 13:44.996
I wonder if I can tell you

13:44.997 --> 13:47.999
one of my deepest sexual fantasies?

13:48.000 --> 13:50.001
All right. Let me just burp
through my nose for a second,

13:50.002 --> 13:51.369
I've been drinking seltzer.

13:52.772 --> 13:54.005
Okay, what do you got?

13:54.006 --> 13:56.141
Well, you're going
to think this is silly,

13:56.142 --> 13:58.710
but I love it when a man confesses

13:58.711 --> 14:01.379
to manufacturing improprieties.

14:01.380 --> 14:04.316
Oh, yeah? Well, then,
you're gonna love this.

14:04.317 --> 14:06.918
I ordered the brewery
to start making beer cans

14:06.919 --> 14:10.288
out of toxic, unsafe metal,
just to save a few bucks.

14:10.289 --> 14:12.190
Exactly what I wanted to hear.

14:12.191 --> 14:13.624
Thank you, Carter.

14:14.460 --> 14:15.894
And there you have it,

14:15.895 --> 14:17.896
Channel Five News audience.

14:17.897 --> 14:21.132
This has been Tricia Takanawa,
with my undercover expos├й

14:21.133 --> 14:23.501
of Pawtucket Patriot Brewery.

14:23.502 --> 14:26.871
Up next... is Papa John dyeing
his eyebrows?

14:26.872 --> 14:28.873
I sleep with him to find out,

14:28.874 --> 14:31.810
though I'm fairly confident
the answer is yes.

14:31.811 --> 14:33.712
And... we're clear.

14:33.713 --> 14:35.480
What-What's going on?

14:35.481 --> 14:37.649
I finished my investigation.

14:37.650 --> 14:38.984
But... I don't understand.

14:38.985 --> 14:40.919
I... I thought we were in love.

14:40.920 --> 14:42.593
I only let you think that.

14:42.594 --> 14:43.521
I'm sorry.

14:43.522 --> 14:45.623
It's time for me to go.

14:48.227 --> 14:49.060
Chris?

14:49.061 --> 14:50.295
Hi, Grandpa.

14:50.296 --> 14:51.896
I got an internship.

14:51.897 --> 14:54.432
You mean, you've been
working for Tricia?

14:54.433 --> 14:57.034
Hang on, I got to get
20 seconds of room tone.

14:58.137 --> 14:59.938
What's room tone?

14:59.939 --> 15:01.438
Oh, we got to start again.

15:06.508 --> 15:08.799
I miss her so much, Griffin.

15:08.800 --> 15:11.782
Of all the women I've
institutionalized Babs over,

15:11.783 --> 15:13.970
she's the one who meant the most to me.

15:13.971 --> 15:14.885
I know.

15:14.886 --> 15:16.787
It's like, one day she's my Tiger Mom,

15:16.788 --> 15:18.455
and the next day she isn't,

15:18.456 --> 15:19.923
and the day before that first day,

15:19.924 --> 15:21.290
she also wasn't.

15:21.292 --> 15:23.293
But the point is she hurt us, Carter.

15:23.294 --> 15:25.028
We got to get her back.

15:25.029 --> 15:26.964
We need revenge.

15:28.800 --> 15:30.033
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

15:30.034 --> 15:31.201
Coming up next,

15:31.202 --> 15:34.404
Nicki Minaj... is a bear?

15:34.405 --> 15:37.975
But first, congratulations to
our very own Tricia Takanawa.

15:37.976 --> 15:39.977
That's right, Tom.
Tricia's recent expos├й

15:39.978 --> 15:41.712
on the Pawtucket Patriot Brewery

15:41.713 --> 15:43.380
has been nominated for a local Emmy.

15:43.381 --> 15:45.582
Mm, the "local" really hurts that.

15:45.583 --> 15:46.917
That's it, Griffin.

15:46.918 --> 15:48.619
That's how we'll get our revenge.

15:48.620 --> 15:50.354
You and I will go to the local Emmys,

15:50.355 --> 15:52.022
and we'll embarrass Tricia
on her big night

15:52.023 --> 15:53.457
in front of all her peers.

15:53.458 --> 15:55.092
That's a great idea!

15:55.093 --> 15:56.426
'Cause people need to know

15:56.427 --> 15:57.828
that she's an even bigger fraud

15:57.829 --> 15:59.463
than Robert Baden Powell,

15:59.464 --> 16:01.231
the founder of the Boy Scouts.

16:01.232 --> 16:03.500
Ma'am, I'd like to take
your son into the woods.

16:03.501 --> 16:05.969
What? That sounds suspicious.

16:05.970 --> 16:08.438
Well, what if I said we'd
both be wearing shorts

16:08.439 --> 16:10.474
and neckerchiefs, and
I'd give him little patches

16:10.475 --> 16:12.308
for doing what I say?

16:18.383 --> 16:19.983
So? How'd we do?

16:19.984 --> 16:21.518
Did you pass your driver's test?

16:21.519 --> 16:22.919
Uh, yeah. Yeah, I think so.

16:22.920 --> 16:24.154
You brought up IPDE?

16:24.155 --> 16:25.455
As a matter of fact, I did.

16:25.456 --> 16:26.556
He was impressed?

16:26.557 --> 16:28.291
No, he had no idea
what I was talking about.

16:28.292 --> 16:29.626
He tried to Google it on his phone

16:29.627 --> 16:31.862
and ended up spilling hot coffee
on his balls.

16:31.863 --> 16:33.764
I took him to the ER
and he said he'd pass me

16:33.765 --> 16:35.232
if I picked him up in an hour.

16:35.233 --> 16:36.867
So it did work.

16:36.868 --> 16:39.202
Well, congratulations, you're
getting your license back!

16:39.203 --> 16:40.570
I know, it's great.

16:40.571 --> 16:43.306
Now I'll be able to go to
those dog parties again.

17:10.468 --> 17:11.701
There's Tricia.

17:13.438 --> 17:15.238
Sweet. What's our plan??

17:15.239 --> 17:17.007
We put this in her drink.

17:17.008 --> 17:19.876
It'll make her instantly
"triple" herself.

17:19.877 --> 17:22.546
Tripling is when you vomit,
defecate, and orgasm,

17:22.547 --> 17:24.047
all at the same time.

17:24.048 --> 17:25.749
Wha... I-I don't...

17:25.750 --> 17:27.422
Why would that medicine even exist?

17:27.423 --> 17:28.251
Cosby.

17:28.252 --> 17:29.686
Now all we need is a distraction

17:29.687 --> 17:31.221
so we can spike her cocktail.

17:31.222 --> 17:32.989
Aha. You leave that to me.

17:32.990 --> 17:34.591
I know something that might distract

17:34.592 --> 17:36.159
all these news people.

17:36.160 --> 17:37.794
Maybe if one of us just chuckles

17:37.795 --> 17:39.162
for no apparent reason,

17:39.163 --> 17:40.797
everyone else will start chuckling.

17:40.798 --> 17:42.032
Worth a shot.

17:51.409 --> 17:52.809
All right, they're all news chuckling!

17:52.810 --> 17:54.044
Go, go, go!

18:02.053 --> 18:03.887
Okay. All Tricia's got to do now

18:03.888 --> 18:05.322
is take one sip and she'll blow it out

18:05.323 --> 18:06.590
of all three holes,

18:06.591 --> 18:07.991
right here in front of everyone.

18:07.992 --> 18:11.093
And that will make us feel
better about our life choices.

18:11.996 --> 18:13.230
Hello, Mother.

18:13.231 --> 18:15.165
I'm so happy you could be here tonight.

18:15.166 --> 18:16.433
Why happy?

18:16.434 --> 18:17.768
You no work for Channel Ten,

18:17.769 --> 18:19.035
just Channel Five.

18:19.036 --> 18:20.537
Only half as good.

18:20.538 --> 18:22.906
Mother, please,
I-I'm being honored tonight.

18:22.907 --> 18:25.342
What honor? Connie Chung
marry Maury Povich,

18:25.343 --> 18:27.244
form media super team.

18:27.245 --> 18:29.713
Where your Povich? You have no Povich.

18:29.714 --> 18:32.749
Wow. Tricia's mom is really
coming down hard on her.

18:32.750 --> 18:35.252
Yeah, and with really
outdated references.

18:35.253 --> 18:36.620
You know,

18:36.621 --> 18:39.489
it's no wonder Mama Trish
was so tough on me.

18:39.490 --> 18:41.091
It's the only thing she knows.

18:41.092 --> 18:42.592
And where grandchildren?

18:42.593 --> 18:45.395
Who take care of me
when I 121 years old?

18:45.396 --> 18:47.864
Who take care of Irene? No one.

18:47.865 --> 18:49.766
No one take care of Irene.

18:49.767 --> 18:51.268
I guess her name is Irene.

18:51.269 --> 18:53.837
Carter, I-I'm starting
to feel bad for Tricia.

18:53.838 --> 18:56.293
Maybe what she did to us
was wrong, but sheesh,

18:56.294 --> 18:58.742
look what her own life has been like.

18:58.743 --> 19:00.644
I-I don't, I don't think I can do this.

19:00.645 --> 19:02.879
Well, this stuff's already in her drink.

19:09.153 --> 19:12.588
Mama Tricia!

19:16.394 --> 19:19.762
No!

19:29.440 --> 19:32.309
Where'd you get these?

19:32.310 --> 19:35.477
Oh, I see the guy.

19:38.616 --> 19:39.850
You're a weird guy, Griffin.

19:39.851 --> 19:41.051
Eh, I don't know.

19:41.052 --> 19:42.419
You know, I just been thinking,

19:42.420 --> 19:44.654
the way you and me fell
so fast for this lady,

19:44.655 --> 19:46.189
and for no reason?

19:46.190 --> 19:48.283
Maybe the problem ain't
Tricia, you know?

19:48.284 --> 19:49.494
Maybe it's us.

19:49.495 --> 19:50.260
What do you mean?

19:50.261 --> 19:52.162
Well, with my real mom gone,

19:52.163 --> 19:54.130
I-I guess maybe I just needed

19:54.131 --> 19:56.066
someone in my life to fill that role.

19:56.067 --> 20:00.003
Someone who loves me enough to
call me fat and lazy and stupid.

20:00.004 --> 20:02.272
Hmm, maybe you're right.

20:02.273 --> 20:05.909
And maybe I was just looking
for a way to feel young again.

20:05.910 --> 20:09.346
Hey, Carter? We're gonna be okay.

20:13.217 --> 20:15.919
Ah, crap. This thing was a rental.

20:15.920 --> 20:17.453
Here's your tux back, bye!

20:21.425 --> 20:23.426
Well, I'm just glad all this nonsense

20:23.427 --> 20:25.328
with Tricia Takanawa is over.

20:25.329 --> 20:27.097
Hey, what ever happened with Grandma?

20:27.098 --> 20:28.899
Yeah, that's what everybody
was thinking about, Meg.

20:28.900 --> 20:30.934
Trust me, she'll come back
if we need her.

20:30.935 --> 20:32.102
Hey, Stewie, seriously,

20:32.103 --> 20:33.270
thanks for everything you did

20:33.271 --> 20:34.504
to help me get my license back.

20:34.505 --> 20:35.805
My pleasure.

20:35.806 --> 20:37.307
But now you owe me.

20:37.308 --> 20:38.608
That means one day,

20:38.609 --> 20:40.543
I'm gonna come to you
and ask for a favor.

20:40.544 --> 20:42.078
But I need to know something.

20:42.079 --> 20:43.947
I need to know that you're gonna say yes

20:43.948 --> 20:45.215
when that day comes.

20:45.216 --> 20:47.217
Uh, o-okay.

20:47.218 --> 20:48.585
Can we go for ice cream?

20:53.673 --> 20:54.657
Come on!

20:54.720 --> 20:56.720
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru